hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1028","Yusuf ibn Musa and Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, h. Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us. That is, Ibn Iyadh, on the authority of Mansour, H. Abu Musa and Yaqoub Al-Dawrqi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad Abu Abd narrated to us. Al-Samad, Mansour narrated to us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, h, Abu Musa narrated to us as well Abu Dawud also told us something similar, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer, adding or subtracting from the prayer, then he turned to us with his face, and we said: O Messenger of God, it happened in Is prayer something? He said: “What is that?” So we mentioned to him what he had done, so he bent his leg and faced the Qiblah, and prostrated two prostrations, then he turned to us and said: “If it happened during prayer I told you something, but I am human. I forget just as you forget, so if I forget, remind me. And whoever of you has doubts about his prayer, let him see if that is better. This is the hadith of Abu Musa on the authority of Abd al-Rahman. Abu Musa said: Ibn Mahdi said: So I asked Sufyan about him, and he said: I heard it from Mansour, but I do not remember it. Ahmad ibn Abdah did not mention in his hadith: investigation, and he said: “Whoever of you has made a mistake in his prayer and does not know how long he has prayed, let him say the salutation, then prostrate.” “The two prostrations of forgetfulness.” Abu Bakr said: In this report, if he based his intention on certainty, he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salutation, and this is what I say, and if he based his intention, at least he prostrated You performed the prostration of forgetfulness before greeting the salaam, according to the report of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, and it is not permissible for my origin to refute one of the two reports with the other. Rather, it is necessary to use Every news in its place. Determination means that the heart of the praying person is more inclined to one of the two numbers, and construction is at least an issue other than the question of determination, so one must use Both stories are based on what was narrated in them"
